{{also|fallopian tube}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|fallopian tube}}

===Etymology===
Early 18th century: from {{suf|en|[[w:Gabriele Falloppio|Fallopius]]|an|t1=[[latinized]] form of the name of {{w|Gabriele Falloppio}} (1523 – October 9, 1562), the [[Italian]] [[anatomist]] and [[physician]] who first described them}} + [[tube]] ({{translit|en|it|tuba|nocap=1}}).
[[File:Gray1161.png|thumb|Illustration of the fallopian tube and ovary.]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} Either of the two ducts in female [[mammal]]s through which [[ova]] pass from the [[ovary|ovaries]] to the [[uterus]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|gonaduct}}
* {{l|en|oviduct}}
* {{l|en|salpinx}}
* {{l|en|uterine tube}}

